            <ArticleTitle>[Neuro-rheumatologic manifestations in patients infected with the AIDS virus].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>519-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We are reporting 3 cases of lumbo-radiculalgia, simulating the usual picture of herniated disc, and revealing complications related to the virus of acquired human immunodeficiency (HIV). Rheumatologists must be aware of any atypical clinical signs in patients suffering from lumboradicular disease, and search for a HIV infection.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
